# CSCE 553 Mini Shop Database Indexing Performance Report

*SQL execution plans and HTTP benchmark evaluation*

Prepared for the course instructor and Mini Shop project team
27 October 2026

## 1 Findings and scope

Two targeted indexes are justified as candidates for the order retrieval workload. The reported warmed standalone orders SQL execution time fell from approximately 5.97 ms to 1.19 ms, while the order-items join changed from a full scan and hash join to indexed lookups. The HTTP experiments show a smaller observed difference and do not establish a causal effect or a proven minimum index set.

The no-new-index baseline has one run. The both-index configuration has three runs, whose orders p95 values are 2.83, 2.60 and 2.27 seconds. Their arithmetic mean is 2.567 seconds, 13.3% below the single baseline value of 2.96 seconds. Every measured endpoint p95 remains above the 200 ms target.

