Baseline means neither experimental index is installed; primary-key, unique and other existing indexes are retained. The workload uses the same five endpoint categories, a local Uvicorn application with a FastAPI backend, and remote Supabase PostgreSQL. k6 reports 8 virtual users and a 60-second scenario; wall-clock totals include completion time beyond the scenario duration.

Reported scale is approximately 5,000 products, 60,000 orders and 148,000 order items. These counts describe the experiment context rather than a newly verified database snapshot. The exact application revision, machine specification, database tier, region and cache state should be recorded in a follow-up replication.

## 3 SQL analysis and index rationale

The composite B-tree index on orders(user_id, created_at DESC) aligns with equality filtering by user_id and descending creation-time ordering. The order_items(order_id) index supports lookup of items for selected orders. These indexes address separate stages of order retrieval.

